{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1370408-bloodline-homebrew-new-take-on-the-cockscomb-society-nosferatu","id":1370408,"title":"[Bloodline Homebrew] New take on the Cockscomb Society (Nosferatu)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-25T11:27:34-08:00","id":1370408,"title":"[Bloodline Homebrew] New take on the Cockscomb Society (Nosferatu)","content":"I'm a big fan of the Chronicles of Darkness as well as the Victorian Era. They both speak to me in many ways. It is therefore no secret that I love products like Victorian Lost for Changeling: the Lost and Lifting the Veil found in Dark Eras: Companion. It also means I'm a big fan of some of the Victorian-themed Vampire: the Requiem bloodlines.<br /> <br /> As of recently, I've been creating my own Victorian Era supplement for Vampire: the Requiem, Second Edition. It will contain my ideas for Vampire: the Requiem in the Victorian Era, it will contain entirely new art (mostly made by myself) and it will contain Victorian-themed bloodlines, some of which are converted from the previous edition of Vampire: the Requiem It will be published on the Storytellers Vault when it's finished, but for now, I want to give you a sneak peek for one of the bloodlines I reinvented.<br /> <br /> I introduce to you: my take on the Cockscomb Society, both a Victorian hellfire club and Nosferatu bloodline:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cYou think I\u2019m haunting? My, that is not something one says to a gentleman. Very well, it is decided, you will stay for the night and teach me how to be as impeccable as you are. Don\u2019t get the wrong idea, your consent is not required. I will take your best qualities and add them to mine. I will seize them from you, like picking a beautiful orchid and adding it to my bouquet. The only choice you have in the matter is whether we do this the easy way or the hard way.\u201d</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> \u2014 Sir Hector Strachan, member of London\u2019s Cockscomb Society</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Something dead approaches. It promises to show you a good time. You know something is off, but you don\u2019t want to refuse. It is a walking contradiction. Proper, clean and well-mannered, yet offensive, grotesque and brutal. It is the most beautiful hideous thing you\u2019ve ever seen. You think it wants something from you, but you're wrong; it doesn\u2019t want something, it wants everything. It wants to feel alive, but it has no life of its own, so it will take yours.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Called the Cockscomb Ladies, Gents, Roosters, or simply Leeches, the members of the Cockscomb Society embody the hypocrisy of Victorian society. Most Victorian gentlemen are obsessed with propriety, status, and morality, always keeping up appearances when in polite company, but when the curtains are closed and the lights are out, these same gentlemen can be found seeking perverse pleasures in the hellfire clubs of London, where they smoke opium, drink absinthe and fornicate with exotic women. The Cockscomb Society\u2014both a hellfire club and Nosferatu bloodline\u2014is no different. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Cockscomb Ladies and Gents are Haunts who have learned to present themselves as the finest gentlemen England has to offer. Dapper and genteel, they talk the talk and walk the walk. They have forgone their clan\u2019s ways of brutality and terror in favor of a refined deft touch. They refuse to be isolated, refuse to be outsiders, refuse to let their clan\u2019s curse define them. But don\u2019t be fooled, underneath the pretty face and politeness lurks your worst nightmare. Like Sweeny Todd and Dorian Gray, the Cockscomb Society is a horror story straight out of a penny dreadful. </span></span> </div> </div> </div>You can read the rest in this Google Drive document: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NGAci06SVY-1C_rEqVh6_vD47WuIAIsT-aeY2nH8I30/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Feedback is welcome. I'm especially curious about what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar192_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"192\" data-vbnamecard=\"192\">Yossarian</a> might have to say!<br /> <br /> Thank you in advance and feel free to use this reimagining of the Cockscomb Society at your tables!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T12:47:42-08:00","id":1370425,"title":"","content":"Very nice! I like the Seized Talent condition in particular as a new take on vampirism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T12:52:27-08:00","id":1370426,"title":"","content":"I really like it! Cool twist on the original. The only thing I'd alter is the leeching talent effect: I think it should have a cost or a drawback. Negating your clan bane is pretty good, especially the Nosferatu curse, so I feel like there should be consequences to that. Also, wholly positive Conditions tend not to be persistent, and don't usually have a Beat criteria.<br /> <br /> Also, I like that you added an option for Kindred members with the fifth dot of the Mystery Cult Initiation. I wish I'd done that with the Icelus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T13:12:27-08:00","id":1370429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1370408-bloodline-homebrew-new-take-on-the-cockscomb-society-nosferatu?p=1370426#post1370426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like it! Cool twist on the original. The only thing I'd alter is the leeching talent effect: I think it should have a cost or a drawback. Negating your clan bane is pretty good, especially the Nosferatu curse, so I feel like there should be consequences to that. Also, wholly positive Conditions tend not to be persistent, and don't usually have a Beat criteria.<br /> <br /> Also, I like that you added an option for Kindred members with the fifth dot of the Mystery Cult Initiation. I wish I'd done that with the Icelus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the feedback! Very useful, exactly what I hoped for!<br /> <br /> The Seized Talent Condition isn't really persistent in so far that it fades away after a number of nights, but so do Conditions like Bestial and Wanton, yet they're still called Persistent, so I see where you're coming from.<br /> <br /> Based on your feedback, I will remove the Beat criteria, to start with. What would be a good negative consequence to add to the Condition? A Breaking Point? It does seem logical for this act to be a breaking point since you're literally giving your Nosferatu curse to someone else, that's pretty monstrous. Do you agree?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T13:22:14-08:00","id":1370431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tomorrow's Nobody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1370408-bloodline-homebrew-new-take-on-the-cockscomb-society-nosferatu?p=1370429#post1370429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the feedback! Very useful, exactly what I hoped for!<br /> <br /> The Seized Talent Condition isn't really persistent in so far that it fades away after a number of nights, but so do Conditions like Bestial and Wanton, yet they're still called Persistent, so I see where you're coming from.<br /> <br /> Based on your feedback, I will remove the Beat criteria, to start with. What would be a good negative consequence to add to the Condition? A Breaking Point? It does seem logical for this act to be a breaking point since you're literally giving your Nosferatu curse to someone else, that's pretty monstrous. Do you agree?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, a breaking point would be good, maybe at whatever the character's current Humanity is. It makes the whole thing a little riskier, and it means they start relying on the effect more and more as they lose Humanity to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}